# Finite word table for the fixed star candidate

The 1024 words and four transition tables were discovered by breadth-first
multiplication of the four fixed permutations in `SylowData`. This module
only defines data. `Coverage` certifies every transition and derives exhaustive
coverage by induction on the generated subgroup. No cardinality is assumed.

Source: the candidate fixed in `../source/sylow.json`; reflection script
`source/generate.py` in this directory. Indices are split into 32 blocks solely
to keep kernel reduction of the tables inexpensive.
-/

